      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Trifluoperazine, a lipophilic basic amine with a tricyclic aromatic system, was detected in brain despite dose-limiting toxicity and is considered to cross the BBB by passive diffusion, supporting CNS access for similarly lipophilic basic amines.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "Compound 16f showed a brain penetration index of 3.5 (AUCbrain/plasma) in rats, demonstrating good brain exposure for a lipophilic heteroaromatic amine and supporting the query's predicted CNS penetration.",
